    "content": "View all Hollywood, Florida, is renowned for its 7 miles of pristine sandy beaches and the iconic 2.5-mile Hollywood Beach Broadwalk, a brick-paved oceanfront promenade lined with restaurants, shops, and cafes. Located between Miami and Fort Lauderdale, it is also known for its historic downtown, the artsy ArtsPark at Young Circle, and a relaxed, classic Florida vibe. Key Highlights and Attractions: Hollywood Beach Broadwalk: A top attraction designated as a nostalgic promenade featuring bicycle rentals, cafes, and easy access to the ocean. Downtown Hollywood: Features a vibrant, walkable, and historic district with arts and culture, including the ArtsPark at Young Circle. ArtsPark at Young Circle Outdoor Activities: The city boasts over 60 parks, seven golf courses, and the Anne Kolb Nature Center, a 1,500-acre coastal mangrove wetland. Anne Kolb Nature Center Margaritaville Hollywood Beach Resort: A major, popular resort right on the beach. Yellow Green Farmers Market: A large, popular indoor market focusing on local food and artisan products. Hollywood Dog Beach: A specific, popular section of the beach allowing dogs. Location: Conveniently located near the Fort Lauderdale-Hollywood International Airport and the Seminole Hard Rock Hotel & Casino (\"Guitar Hotel\"). Seminole Hard Rock Hotel & Casino (\"Guitar Hotel\") According to Facebook users on the Best of Hollywood Beach group, the Broadwalk is highly valued for its walkability, though some users note it can get crowded during peak times. Facebook users on the Best of Hollywood Beach group",
